      "proposition": "The majority will hold that Williamson County finality does not bar adjudication of alleged completed injuries from coercive threats and discriminatory permitting demands merely because the dispute involves land use; ordinary Article III injury principles, rather than an automatic requirement to obtain a final permit decision, govern those claims."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "ground-breadth",
      "proposition": "The majority will limit its ruling to claims alleging injury independent of the eventual zoning decision, leaving intact a finality requirement where the asserted injury depends on what land use officials ultimately permit, rather than exempting every First Amendment or RLUIPA land-use claim from finality."
    }
